 "9602": {
  "en": [
   "On the petals of my garland's flowers is written",
   "the spell-script of spring.",
   "In its sweetness lies youth's invitation.",
   "The Sahana melody is",
   "dyed in its crimson hue,",
   "the honeybee's hunger, in unheard rhythm,",
   "hums in its fragrance.",
   "Bring the basket, weave the garland,",
   "bring madhabi, malati, ashoka sprays,",
   "come, all of you, come.",
   "Bring oleander, rangan, kanchan, tuberose,",
   "jasmine in full bloom,",
   "come, all of you, come.",
   "Wear the garland, wear the garland, lovely one,",
   "make haste, oh make haste.",
   "Tonight, on the full-moon night, the moon is waking,",
   "the bakul grove",
   "sways and trembles in the south wind,",
   "shivering with a soft murmur.",
   "The dancing forest-woman drifts through the forest court,",
   "round her restless feet her anklets hum.",
   "Do not let the honeyed night stream by in vain,",
   "listless one, alas.",
   "Once the auspicious hour has gone it will not be caught again,",
   "the store of nectar",
   "it will empty into the dust,",
   "the banjul sprays will wither.",
   "In the night anointed with moonbeams, in cricket-loud forest shade,",
   "in the south breeze cooing with the sleepless koel's cry of parting,",
   "my garden filled with flowers, flowers, flowers,",
   "the kingshuk boughs turned restless, swaying, swaying."
  ],
